#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cqcc: the CQ compiler driver (cq-w1-driver).

    clang -O1 -include CQ.h, per C translation unit
      -> with several units, CQ_K / CQ_K2 bound per unit by C scope (CR §0, cq-z9vt; bind_k_per_unit): a line naming
         a function some unit defines becomes its attribute "cq-k" / "cq-k2"; differing lines are warned about
      -> llvm-link of the user units, then the injection bundle (bundle/manifest.json) --only-needed,
         only when the linked user module needs it (the bundle rule below)
      -> opt -load-pass-plugin=libCQLower.so -passes=cq-lower [-cq-k=...] [-cq-k-default=...]
      -> the lowered module (-S), an object (-c) or an executable linked with the --backend libraries and, when
         the lowered module asks for a __cq_* host symbol, bundle/host/cq_host.c (rulings Q7)
    --cq-check additionally runs `python3 -m cqcheck user` on the linked module and the lowered one.

Usage: cqcc [options] inputs...

Inputs, by suffix:
  .c .i              compiled with clang -O1 -include CQ.h (one translation unit each)
  .cpp .cc .cxx      compiled with clang++ -O1 -fno-exceptions -include driver/cq.hpp (CQ.h's surface as overloads);
                     the pass has no lowering for invoke/landingpad, so -fexceptions is an internal error at a throw
  .ll .bc            an -O1 IR unit, linked as given (e.g. a corpus name.O1.ll)
  .o .a .dylib .so   handed to the final link only (executable output)

Output (one of; default: an executable):
  -S                 the lowered module as textual IR (default name a.lowered.ll)
  -c                 an object file (default a.o); with -emit-llvm, the lowered module as bitcode (a.bc)
  -o FILE            output path
The whole program is one module (NORTHSTAR principle 3): -c makes one object from every input.

Options:
  -cq-k=<fn>=<k>,...   per-function loop cutoff, passed through to cq-lower (repeatable)
  -cq-k-default=<k>    global loop cutoff, passed through to cq-lower
  -cq-k2=<fn>=<k>,...  -cq-k2-default=<k>   the K2 byte bound (CR §0), passed through to cq-lower
  -cq-no-output        in the functions lowered here, a call of a stream-output function (printf, fprintf, puts,
                       fwrite, ...; not sprintf/snprintf) that the inputs do not define fails as on a closed stream:
                       its error value, no output and no formatting circuit. For a library whose error paths print
                       (GSL); not for building the C library
  --cq-roots FILE      a root list (rule 27), one C function name per line, passed through to cq-lower; one list per
                       run. In a program, a listed function with no body in
                       the inputs is lowered code of a linked library: only its call is lowered, to the declared clone
                       __cq_q_<fn>_<mask>_t of the call's arrangement (rule 27), and the bundle never supplies its
                       body. A call with every actual classical where no cell can be QUANTUM stays the C call (the
                       original library's symbol, rule 16). A line that is a clone name
                       (CR §1.4) asks cq-lower for that clone as well.
  --cq-ext-roots FILE  the root list of another lowered library this build calls (repeatable): its functions are
                       calls of that library's clones, as --cq-roots names in a program; a --cq-lib build does not
                       export them and never takes their bodies from the bundle
  --cq-lib             build a lowered library: with --cq-roots, every listed function is a root. Its body comes from
                       the inputs or, when they have none, from the bundle; its table clones, one per argument
                       arrangement the C signature gives (rule 27: every mask up to 5 scalar formals, else one per
                       set of the classes pointer, integer, floating point), their _ctl forms and twins are
                       exported. A library built before arrangements exports all-ones only: rebuild it. Output is an object (-c, the default), an archive when -o ends in .a, or
                       IR (-S). Inputs are optional. A program names the same list and links the library, then the
                       original (natively compiled) library, e.g. --backend libq.a --backend libnative.a (rule 27):
                       the lowered library exports its table clones only and defines no C symbol. Every C function
                       is the original's (a root's lowered body is internal, -cq-host-roots to cq-lower; its row is
                       keyed by the original's address); every external global of the inputs is only declared, the
                       original's object (rule 20); what the bundle supplies beside the roots is internal.
  --backend LIB        a backend library for the final link: a path, -lname or -Ldir (repeatable)
  --no-softfloat       do not link the compiler's float templates (softfloat/build/libqsoftfloat*.a, linked after
                       the backend when built): the backend then defines every cq_template_f* itself
  --cq-check           run `cqcheck user` (the C-oracle check) on the result; its exit status is cqcc's
  --cq-entry FN        the entry function for --cq-check (default main)
  --cq-samples N       passed to cqcheck user as --samples
  --save-temps DIR     keep the units, linked.ll (the pass input) and lowered.ll in DIR
  -v                   print every command before running it
  -I.. -D.. -U.. -include FILE -isystem DIR -std=.. -W.. -w -f..   passed to the C compile
  -Xclang-cc ARG       one more argument for the C compile

Environment: CQ_SPEC_DIR (default spec/; CQ.h is read from it), CQ_BUILD_DIR (default build/),
CQ_PLUGIN (default $CQ_BUILD_DIR/pass/libCQLower.so), CQ_LLVM_BIN (default /usr/local/opt/llvm@19/bin),
CQ_BUNDLE_MANIFEST (default bundle/manifest.json; its entries are relative to its own directory).

The bundle rule (cq-jxaw; the checker applies the same rule, cq-b041). Let U be the module llvm-link made
of the user units (or the single unit as given) and B the set of external symbols the bundle files define
(llvm-nm --defined-only --extern-only over every manifest file). The bundle is linked iff some symbol of
B is declared in U without a body (llvm-nm --undefined-only of U, which lists every external
declaration, used or not, and no intrinsic). Then, and only then: llvm-link -S U --only-needed
<manifest files, in manifest order>. Otherwise U goes to the pass untouched, so a module that needs
nothing from the bundle is lowered exactly as without one (CLAUDE.md Pipeline, NORTHSTAR principle 1:
llvm-link would otherwise rename source_filename, reorder declarations and append the bundle's named
metadata). A weak or linkonce definition in U is a body, not a declaration. Names are compared as
llvm-nm prints them (Mach-O mangled) on both sides.

Before the bundle rule, the result entries (owner ruling 2026-11-12; bundle/recipe.json "entries"): when U calls a
C library output function whose result the pass computes by a bundle entry (driver/cq_entries.py), the entry's
declaration is linked into U from a unit that also lists it in @llvm.compiler.used (as for the libm names), so U
declares a bundle symbol, the entry's body is linked and kept. U is unchanged otherwise.

Lowered libraries (rule 27, BACKEND_ABI §3; cq-ywi8o). One root list serves both sides:

    cqcc --cq-lib --cq-roots libm.roots -o libqm.a         # lower cos, sin, ... once (bodies from the bundle)
    cqcc prog.c --cq-roots libm.roots -L. -lqm -lbackend   # prog's calls of them are calls of the library's clones

In the program build the listed names are removed from the bundle first (opt -passes=cq-drop-bodies on a scratch
copy of each bundle file that defines one), so neither the bundle rule nor the libm declarations nor a body another
injected function pulls in can bring a listed body back: the library's is the only one. bundle/host/cq_host.c is
linked whenever a root list is given, since the library asks for the host symbols even when the program does not.
--cq-check of such a program names the listed functions to the checker (CQ_ROOTS_EXTRA): they are its stand-ins on
both sides, so the program's own lowering is checked, not the library's.

A failing step exits with that step's status and writes no output. A failing --cq-check still writes
the output and exits with cqcheck user's status.
"""
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
from pathlib import Path

sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))
import cq_entries  # noqa: E402  (driver/cq_entries.py: the result entries a program needs before its link)

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
LLVM_BIN = Path(os.environ.get("CQ_LLVM_BIN", "/usr/local/opt/llvm@19/bin"))
SPEC_DIR = Path(os.environ.get("CQ_SPEC_DIR", str(ROOT / "spec")))
BUILD_DIR = Path(os.environ.get("CQ_BUILD_DIR", str(ROOT / "build")))
PLUGIN = Path(os.environ.get("CQ_PLUGIN", str(BUILD_DIR / "pass" / "libCQLower.so")))
MANIFEST = Path(os.environ.get("CQ_BUNDLE_MANIFEST", str(ROOT / "bundle" / "manifest.json"))).resolve()

C_SUFFIXES = {".c", ".i"}
CXX_SUFFIXES = {".cpp", ".cc", ".cxx"}
CXX_HEADER = Path(__file__).resolve().parent / "cq.hpp"
IR_SUFFIXES = {".ll", ".bc"}
LINK_SUFFIXES = {".o", ".a", ".dylib", ".so", ".tbd"}
HOST_SOURCE = ROOT / "bundle" / "host" / "cq_host.c"
# The compiler's float templates (BACKEND_ABI §2.12): softfloat/build.sh lib [softfloat/cqsf_f80.roots] makes them.
FLOAT_LIBS = [ROOT / "softfloat" / "build" / n for n in ("libqsoftfloat.a", "libqsoftfloat_f80.a")]
HOST_SYMBOLS = {"__cq_mem", "__cq_alloc", "__cq_sig", "__cq_clone_register", "__cq_clone_resolve", "__cq_clone_count",
                "__cq_clone_at", "__cq_object", "__cq_unbound", "__cq_pointer"}

VERBOSE = False


class DriverError(Exception):
    def __init__(self, msg: str, status: int = 1):
        super().__init__(msg)
        self.status = status


def usage(msg: str) -> "DriverError":
    return DriverError(f"cqcc: {msg} (cqcc --help for usage)", 2)


def tool(name: str) -> str:
    p = LLVM_BIN / name
    if not p.exists():
        raise DriverError(f"cqcc: {p} not found (brew llvm@19; CQ_LLVM_BIN overrides)")
    return str(p)


def run(cmd, what: str, **kw) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:
    if VERBOSE:
        print(" ".join(str(c) for c in cmd), file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
    r = subprocess.run([str(c) for c in cmd], **kw)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        raise DriverError(f"cqcc: {what} failed (exit {r.returncode})", r.returncode)
    return r


def parse_args(argv):
    o = {
        "inputs": [], "out": None, "mode": "exe", "emit_llvm": False, "kflags": [], "backend": [],
        "check": False, "entry": "main", "samples": None, "save_temps": None, "cflags": [],
        "roots": None, "ext_roots": [], "lib": False, "mode_given": False, "softfloat": True,
    }
    it = iter(argv)

    def value(flag):
        try:
            return next(it)
        except StopIteration:
            raise usage(f"{flag} needs a value")

    for a in it:
        if a in ("-h", "--help"):
            print(__doc__)
            sys.exit(0)
        elif a == "-o":
            o["out"] = value(a)
        elif a == "-S":
            o["mode"], o["mode_given"] = "S", True
        elif a == "-c":
            o["mode"], o["mode_given"] = "c", True
        elif a == "--cq-lib":
            o["lib"] = True
        elif a == "--no-softfloat":
            o["softfloat"] = False
        elif a == "-emit-llvm":
            o["emit_llvm"] = True
        elif a == "-v":
            global VERBOSE
            VERBOSE = True
        elif a in ("-cq-no-output", "--cq-no-output"):
            o["kflags"].append("-cq-no-output")
        elif a.startswith(("-cq-k2=", "--cq-k2=", "-cq-k2-default=", "--cq-k2-default=")):
            o["kflags"].append("-" + a.lstrip("-"))
        elif a in ("-cq-k2", "--cq-k2", "-cq-k2-default", "--cq-k2-default"):
            o["kflags"].append(f"-{a.lstrip('-')}={value(a)}")
        elif a.startswith(("-cq-k=", "--cq-k=")):
            o["kflags"].append("-cq-k=" + a.split("=", 1)[1])
        elif a.startswith(("-cq-k-default=", "--cq-k-default=")):
            o["kflags"].append("-cq-k-default=" + a.split("=", 1)[1])
        elif a in ("-cq-k", "--cq-k", "-cq-k-default", "--cq-k-default"):
            o["kflags"].append(f"-{a.lstrip('-')}={value(a)}")
        elif a == "--cq-roots" or a.startswith("--cq-roots="):
            if o["roots"] is not None:
                raise usage("--cq-roots given twice (one root list per run)")
            o["roots"] = Path(a.split("=", 1)[1] if "=" in a else value(a)).resolve()
            o["kflags"].append(f"-cq-roots={o['roots']}")
        elif a == "--cq-ext-roots":
            o["ext_roots"].append(Path(value(a)).resolve())
        elif a == "--backend":
            o["backend"].append(value(a))
        elif a.startswith("--backend="):
            o["backend"].append(a.split("=", 1)[1])
        elif a == "--cq-check":
            o["check"] = True
        elif a == "--cq-entry":
            o["entry"] = value(a)
        elif a.startswith("--cq-entry="):
            o["entry"] = a.split("=", 1)[1]
        elif a == "--cq-samples":
            o["samples"] = value(a)
        elif a.startswith("--cq-samples="):
            o["samples"] = a.split("=", 1)[1]
        elif a == "--save-temps":
            o["save_temps"] = value(a)
        elif a.startswith("--save-temps="):
            o["save_temps"] = a.split("=", 1)[1]
        elif a == "-Xclang-cc":
            o["cflags"].append(value(a))
        elif a in ("-I", "-D", "-U", "-include", "-isystem", "-iquote"):
            o["cflags"] += [a, value(a)]
        elif a.startswith(("-I", "-D", "-U", "-std=", "-W", "-f", "-isystem", "-iquote")) or a == "-w":
            o["cflags"].append(a)
        elif a.startswith("-l") or a.startswith("-L"):
            o["backend"].append(a)
        elif a.startswith("-") and a != "-":
            raise usage(f"unknown option {a}")
        else:
            o["inputs"].append(Path(a))
    if o["lib"]:
        if o["roots"] is None:
            raise usage("--cq-lib needs --cq-roots (the functions the library exports)")
        if not o["mode_given"]:
            o["mode"] = "c"
    if not o["inputs"] and not o["lib"]:
        raise usage("no input files")
    if o["roots"] is not None and not o["roots"].exists():
        raise usage(f"--cq-roots {o['roots']}: no such file")
    if o["samples"] is not None and not str(o["samples"]).isdigit():
        raise usage("--cq-samples expects a count")
    for p in o["inputs"]:
        suf = p.suffix
        if suf not in C_SUFFIXES | CXX_SUFFIXES | IR_SUFFIXES | LINK_SUFFIXES:
            raise usage(f"{p}: unknown input kind (expected .c .i .cpp .cc .cxx .ll .bc .o .a .dylib .so .tbd)")
        if not p.exists():
            raise usage(f"{p}: no such file")
    if o["mode"] != "exe" and any(p.suffix in LINK_SUFFIXES for p in o["inputs"]):
        raise usage("object and library inputs only go to the executable link (drop -S/-c)")
    if o["mode"] != "exe" and o["backend"]:
        raise usage("--backend only applies to the executable link (drop -S/-c)")
    if o["emit_llvm"] and o["mode"] != "c":
        raise usage("-emit-llvm goes with -c (bitcode); -S already emits textual IR")
    if o["out"] is None:
        o["out"] = {"S": "a.lowered.ll", "c": "a.bc" if o["emit_llvm"] else "a.o", "exe": "a.out"}[o["mode"]]
    if Path(o["out"]).suffix == ".a" and (not o["lib"] or o["mode"] != "c" or o["emit_llvm"]):
        raise usage("an archive output (-o x.a) is a --cq-lib object build")
    return o


def root_names(roots) -> list:
    """The C names of a root list (rule 27): every line that is not a clone name, in file order, once each."""
    if roots is None:
        return []
    out = []
    for line in roots.read_text().splitlines():
        line = line.strip()
        if line and not line.startswith("__cq_q_") and line not in out:
            out.append(line)
    return out


def bundle_without(bundle, names, work: Path):
    """The bundle with the listed functions as declarations (module docstring, "Lowered libraries"): a scratch copy of
    every file that defines one, the file itself otherwise."""
    out = []
    for i, f in enumerate(bundle):
        defined = {n.removeprefix("_") for n in nm(f, ["--defined-only"], f"llvm-nm of the injection bundle {f.name}", work)}
        drop = [n for n in names if n in defined]
        if not drop:
            out.append(f)
            continue
        g = work / f"bundle{i}.nolisted.ll"
        run([tool("opt"), f"-load-pass-plugin={PLUGIN}", "-passes=cq-drop-bodies", "-cq-drop-bodies=" + ",".join(drop),
             "-S", f, "-o", g], f"opt -passes=cq-drop-bodies on {f.name}")
        out.append(g)
    return out


def target_flags():
    """x86-64 only (NORTHSTAR principle 3). On an x86-64 Mac clang's default triple is what the corpus
    used (x86_64-apple-macosx<version>); anywhere else the triple is forced."""
    r = run([tool("clang"), "-print-target-triple"], "clang -print-target-triple", capture_output=True, text=True)
    return [] if r.stdout.strip().startswith("x86_64-apple-") else ["--target=x86_64-apple-macosx"]


def bundle_files():
    """bundle/manifest.json (cq-w1-bundle's contract, read as checker/cqcheck/oracle.py reads it): a JSON
    list of bitcode paths relative to bundle/ (to the manifest's directory). An empty list is the stub:
    nothing is linked."""
    if not MANIFEST.exists():
        raise DriverError(f"cqcc: {MANIFEST} missing")
    try:
        entries = json.loads(MANIFEST.read_text())
    except ValueError as e:
        raise DriverError(f"cqcc: {MANIFEST}: {e}")
    if not isinstance(entries, list) or not all(isinstance(e, str) for e in entries):
        raise DriverError(f"cqcc: {MANIFEST}: expected a JSON list of paths relative to bundle/")
    files = [(MANIFEST.parent / e).resolve() for e in entries]
    for f in files:
        if not f.exists():
            raise DriverError(f"cqcc: injection bundle file {f} (bundle/manifest.json) missing")
    return files


def nm(path: Path, flags, what: str, work: Path) -> set:
    """External symbol names of an IR file as llvm-nm prints them. llvm-nm reads bitcode only, so a
    textual unit is assembled to a scratch .bc first."""
    if path.suffix == ".ll":
        bc = work / (path.name + ".nm.bc")
        run([tool("llvm-as"), path, "-o", bc], f"llvm-as of {path.name} (bundle rule)")
        path = bc
    r = run([tool("llvm-nm"), *flags, "--extern-only", "--format=just-symbols", path], what,
            capture_output=True, text=True)
    return {ln.strip() for ln in r.stdout.splitlines() if ln.strip()}


def bundle_needed(linked: Path, bundle, work: Path) -> bool:
    """The bundle rule (module docstring): some symbol a bundle file defines is declared in `linked`
    without a body."""
    defined = set()
    for f in bundle:
        defined |= nm(f, ["--defined-only"], f"llvm-nm of the injection bundle {f.name}", work)
    declared = nm(linked, ["--undefined-only"], "llvm-nm of the linked user module", work)
    return bool(defined & declared)


def libm_decls(linked: Path, bundle, work: Path) -> dict:
    """The libm functions the bundle defines that the module's LLVM math intrinsics stand for and no declaration names."""
    defined = set()
    for f in bundle:
        defined |= nm(f, ["--defined-only"], f"llvm-nm of the injection bundle {f.name}", work)
    text = Path(linked).read_text()
    types = {"f32": ("float", "f"), "f64": ("double", ""), "f80": ("x86_fp80", "l")}
    out = {}
    for op, t in re.findall(r"(?m)^declare\b[^@]*@llvm\.(exp|exp2|exp10|log|log2|log10|sin|cos|tan|asin|acos|atan|sinh|cosh|"
                            r"tanh|pow)\.(f32|f64|f80)\(", text):
        ty, sfx = types[t]
        n = op + sfx
        if ("_" + n in defined or n in defined) and not re.search(rf"(?m)^(declare|define)\b[^@]*@{n}\(", text):
            out[n] = f"declare {ty} @{n}({ty}, {ty})\n" if op == "pow" else f"declare {ty} @{n}({ty})\n"
    return out


#                                   CQ_K / CQ_K2 per unit (CR §0, owner ruling 2026-11-15, cq-z9vt)
# A line `CQ_K(f, k)` is clang's `@__cq_k_<f> = internal constant i32 k` in @llvm.used (`CQ_K2`: `@__cq_k2_<f>`, i64).
# It names the f its own unit defines (a static f is that unit's alone), else the external f of that name. For an
# external f the line of the unit defining it wins; where that unit has none, the largest k among the other units'
# lines. llvm-link renames the internal constants (and the statics) independently, so the binding is made per unit,
# before the link: every line bound to a definition becomes the string attribute "cq-k"="k" ("cq-k2") on that
# definition, which the pass's resolveK reads before any constant, and the constant is dropped. "none" marks a
# definition that no line names while some line of its name stays a constant, so resolveK does not read a constant meant
# for another function (K = 0 is a K, owner ruling Q2 of 2026-11-15: the marker is no number). A line naming a function
# no unit defines (a library function, rule 27) stays a constant; resolveK reads it with its llvm-link copies
# __cq_k_<f>.N, the largest k. Only a link of several units is touched: a single unit goes to the pass as clang wrote it.
K_KINDS = (("__cq_k_", "cq-k", "i32", "CQ_K"), ("__cq_k2_", "cq-k2", "i64", "CQ_K2"))
_DEF_RE = re.compile(r'^define\s+([^@\n]*)@(?:"([^"]+)"|([-\w$.]+))\(', re.M)


def _unit_defs(text: str) -> dict:
    """{function name: is_local} of the bodies a unit defines."""
    out = {}
    for m in _DEF_RE.finditer(text):
        out[m.group(2) or m.group(3)] = bool(re.search(r"\b(internal|private)\b", m.group(1)))
    return out


def _unit_lines(text: str, prefix: str, ty: str) -> dict:
    return {m.group(1): int(m.group(2)) for m in
            re.finditer(rf"^@{prefix}([A-Za-z_]\w*) = (?:internal |private )?(?:unnamed_addr )?constant {ty} (-?\d+)\b",
                        text, re.M)}


def _drop_global(text: str, name: str) -> str:
    """The unit without the global @name and without its entry in @llvm.used / @llvm.compiler.used."""
    text = re.sub(rf"^@{re.escape(name)} = [^\n]*\n", "", text, flags=re.M)

    def used(m):
        items = [e for e in m.group(3).split(", ") if e.strip() != f"ptr @{name}"]
        if not items:
            return ""
        return f"{m.group(1)}[{len(items)} x ptr] [{', '.join(items)}]{m.group(4)}"
    return re.sub(r"^(@llvm\.(?:compiler\.)?used = appending global )\[(\d+) x ptr\] \[([^\]\n]*)\]([^\n]*\n)",
                  used, text, flags=re.M)


def _add_fn_attr(text: str, fn: str, attr: str, value) -> str:
    """`define ... @fn(...) [local_]unnamed_addr` followed by `"attr"="value"` among its function attributes."""
    for m in _DEF_RE.finditer(text):
        if (m.group(2) or m.group(3)) != fn:
            continue
        i, depth = m.end() - 1, 0
        while True:   # the closing parenthesis of the parameter list
            c = text[i]
            depth += (c == "(") - (c == ")")
            i += 1
            if depth == 0:
                break
        rest = re.match(r"(?: (?:local_)?unnamed_addr)?(?: addrspace\(\d+\))?", text[i:])
        j = i + rest.end()
        return text[:j] + f' "{attr}"="{value}"' + text[j:]
    return text


def bind_k_per_unit(units, work: Path, names=None):
    """The CQ_K / CQ_K2 binding of several units (comment above), as new unit files where a unit changes. Returns the
    units to link, in the same order."""
    names = names or [u.name for u in units]
    texts = []
    for i, u in enumerate(units):
        if u.suffix == ".bc":
            ll = work / f"unit{i}.{u.stem}.dis.ll"
            run([tool("llvm-dis"), u, "-o", ll], f"llvm-dis of {u.name} (CQ_K binding)")
            u = ll
        texts.append(Path(u).read_text())
    defs = [_unit_defs(t) for t in texts]
    new = list(texts)
    for prefix, attr, ty, macro in K_KINDS:
        lines = [_unit_lines(t, prefix, ty) for t in texts]
        for f in sorted({f for ls in lines for f in ls}):
            ext_def = [u for u in range(len(units)) if defs[u].get(f) is False]
            # the lines naming the external f: those of units that do not define an f of their own
            ext_lines = [(u, lines[u][f]) for u in range(len(units)) if f in lines[u] and f not in defs[u]]
            ext_lines += [(u, lines[u][f]) for u in ext_def if f in lines[u]]
            own = [lines[u][f] for u in ext_def if f in lines[u]]
            others = [lines[u][f] for u in range(len(units)) if f in lines[u] and f not in defs[u]]
            k = max(own) if own else (max(others) if others else None)
            if len({v for _, v in ext_lines}) > 1:
                where = ", ".join(f"{names[u]} {v}" for u, v in ext_lines)
                why = "the line of the unit that defines it" if own else \
                    ("the largest line, no line in the unit that defines it" if ext_def else
                     "the largest line, no unit defines it")
                print(f"cqcc: warning: {macro}({f}, k) differs between units ({where}); {f} gets {k}, {why}",
                      file=sys.stderr)
            kept_const = bool(others) and not ext_def   # lines of a function no unit defines stay constants
            for u in range(len(units)):
                if f in defs[u]:
                    if defs[u][f]:   # a static: its own unit's line only
                        v = lines[u].get(f)
                        if v is not None:
                            new[u] = _add_fn_attr(new[u], f, attr, v)
                        elif kept_const:
                            new[u] = _add_fn_attr(new[u], f, attr, "none")
                    elif k is not None:
                        new[u] = _add_fn_attr(new[u], f, attr, k)
                if f in lines[u] and (f in defs[u] or ext_def):
                    new[u] = _drop_global(new[u], prefix + f)
    out = []
    for i, u in enumerate(units):
        if new[i] == texts[i]:
            out.append(u)
        else:
            p = work / f"k{i}.{u.stem}.ll"
            p.write_text(new[i])
            out.append(p)
    return out


def main(argv) -> int:
    o = parse_args(argv)
    header = SPEC_DIR / "CQ.h"
    if not header.exists():
        raise DriverError(f"cqcc: {header} not found (CQ_SPEC_DIR overrides)")
    if not PLUGIN.exists():
        raise DriverError(f"cqcc: {PLUGIN} not found; build the pass (CQ_PLUGIN overrides)")

    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="cqcc.") as tmpname:
        tmp = Path(tmpname)
        work = Path(o["save_temps"]) if o["save_temps"] else tmp
        work.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)

        # 1. clang -O1 per translation unit.
        tflags = target_flags()
        units, unit_names = [], []
        for i, src in enumerate(o["inputs"]):
            if src.suffix in C_SUFFIXES:
                ll = work / f"unit{i}.{src.stem}.ll"
                run([tool("clang"), "-O1", *tflags, "-include", header, *o["cflags"], "-S", "-emit-llvm",
                     src, "-o", ll], f"clang -O1 {src}")
                units.append(ll)
                unit_names.append(src.name)
            elif src.suffix in CXX_SUFFIXES:
                # shortcut: a -std= flag goes to every unit, so it cannot be given to a mix of C and C++ inputs; split
                # the cflags per language when a program needs that.
                ll = work / f"unit{i}.{src.stem}.ll"
                run([tool("clang++"), "-O1", *tflags, "-fno-exceptions", "-include", CXX_HEADER, *o["cflags"], "-S",
                     "-emit-llvm", src, "-o", ll], f"clang++ -O1 {src}")
                units.append(ll)
                unit_names.append(src.name)
            elif src.suffix in IR_SUFFIXES:
                units.append(src)
                unit_names.append(src.name)
        listed = root_names(o["roots"])
        # --cq-ext-roots: roots of other lowered libraries. cq-lower reads them with the roots (one file); a library
        # build neither exports them nor takes their bodies from the bundle. In a program they are listed names.
        ext = [n for p in o["ext_roots"] for n in root_names(p) if n not in listed]
        if ext:
            both = work / "roots.all.txt"
            both.write_text("".join(p.read_text().rstrip("\n") + "\n" for p in [o["roots"], *o["ext_roots"]] if p))
            o["kflags"] = [f for f in o["kflags"] if not f.startswith("-cq-roots=")] + [f"-cq-roots={both}"]
            if not o["lib"]:
                listed, ext = listed + ext, []
        if not units and o["lib"] and listed:
            # A library made of bundle bodies alone: an empty unit carries the target lines the root stub copies.
            empty_c, empty = work / "empty.c", work / "unit0.empty.ll"
            empty_c.write_text("")
            run([tool("clang"), "-O1", *tflags, "-S", "-emit-llvm", empty_c, "-o", empty], "clang -O1 of an empty unit")
            units.append(empty)
            unit_names.append(empty_c.name)
        if not units:
            raise usage("no C or IR input to lower")

        # 2. llvm-link: the user units in full, then, when the bundle rule (module docstring) says the
        # module needs it, the bundle --only-needed (first file links in full).
        # Everything stays textual IR, as the corpus's name.O1.ll is: bitcode does not keep use-list
        # order, which the pass may observe. A single unit is not relinked: llvm-link would rename its
        # source_filename and reorder its named metadata; the pass then reads exactly what clang wrote.
        linked = work / "linked.ll"
        if len(units) == 1 and units[0].suffix == ".ll":
            shutil.copyfile(units[0], linked)
        else:
            units = bind_k_per_unit(units, work, unit_names)   # CQ_K / CQ_K2 by C scope, before the link (cq-z9vt)
            run([tool("llvm-link"), "-S", *units, "-o", linked], "llvm-link of the user units")
        bundle = bundle_files()
        if ext and bundle:
            bundle = bundle_without(bundle, ext, tmp)
        root_stub = []
        own = nm(linked, ["--defined-only"], "llvm-nm of the linked user module", tmp) if o["lib"] else set()
        if o["lib"]:
            # Rule 27, library build: a root the inputs do not define comes from the bundle. Its declaration, named in
            # @llvm.compiler.used, makes the bundle needed and --only-needed pulls the body and what it calls.
            have = _unit_defs(linked.read_text())
            text = linked.read_text()
            for n in listed:
                if not have.get(n, True):
                    continue   # an externally visible body in the inputs
                # The inputs' own declaration when they have one (the stub and the inputs must agree on the type).
                m = re.search(rf'(?m)^declare\b[^@\n]*@{re.escape(n)}\([^\n]*\)', text)
                decl = re.sub(r'\s+#\d+\b', '', m.group(0)) if m else f"declare void @{n}()"
                root_stub.append((n, decl + "\n"))
        elif listed and bundle:
            bundle = bundle_without(bundle, listed, tmp)
        # The result entries (owner ruling 2026-11-12, cq-cdf9z, cq-m7ftq; driver/cq_entries.py): a deferred output
        # call's result is a call the pass inserts after this link, to a bundle entry. A unit declaring the entries
        # the program's output calls may need, with an @llvm.compiler.used naming them (llvm-link drops an unused
        # declaration), makes the bundle needed and --only-needed pulls their bodies. A program with none is left
        # as it was.
        entries = cq_entries.decls(linked.read_text()) if bundle else []
        libm = libm_decls(linked, bundle, tmp) if bundle else {}
        if bundle and (libm or entries or root_stub or bundle_needed(linked, bundle, tmp)):
            # Rule 18: a math intrinsic is lifted from the libm body the bundle has; its declaration makes it needed.
            extra = []
            text = Path(linked).read_text()
            head = "".join(l + "\n" for l in text.splitlines() if l.startswith(("target datalayout", "target triple")))
            for stem, decl_lines, names in (("libm", list(libm.values()), list(libm)),
                                            ("entries", [d + "\n" for d in entries], cq_entries.names(entries)),
                                            ("roots", [d for _, d in root_stub], [n for n, _ in root_stub])):
                if not names:
                    continue
                used = ", ".join(f"ptr @{n}" for n in names)
                unit = work / f"{stem}.ll"
                unit.write_text(head + "".join(decl_lines) + f"@llvm.compiler.used = appending global [{len(names)} x ptr] "
                                f'[{used}], section "llvm.metadata"\n')
                extra.append(unit)
            run([tool("llvm-link"), "-S", linked, *extra, "--only-needed", *bundle, "-o", linked],
                "llvm-link with the injection bundle")
        if o["lib"]:
            have = _unit_defs(linked.read_text())
            missing = [n for n in listed if have.get(n, True)]
            if missing:
                raise DriverError("cqcc: --cq-lib: no externally visible body in the inputs or the bundle for: "
                                  + ", ".join(missing))
            # What the bundle supplied beside the roots is private to the library: a program that injects the same
            # helper, or a second library, defines its own copy and the link sees one symbol each.
            # Rule 27 (owner ruling 2026-11-21): the original library is linked beside this one and provides every C
            # function (a root the bundle supplied: the host's C library). The lowered library exports its clones only
            # (cq-lower keeps a root's lowered body under a module-internal name).
            if listed:
                o["kflags"].append("-cq-host-roots=" + ",".join(listed))
            keep = work / "lib.exports.txt"
            keep.write_text("".join(n + "\n" for n in sorted({x.removeprefix("_") for x in own} | set(listed))))
            run([tool("opt"), "-S", "-passes=internalize", f"-internalize-public-api-file={keep}", linked, "-o", linked],
                "opt -passes=internalize of the bundle's helpers")

        # 3. The pass, reading the module from stdin so the output does not name a temporary path.
        lowered = work / ("lowered.bc" if o["mode"] == "c" and o["emit_llvm"] else "lowered.ll")
        opt_cmd = [tool("opt"), f"-load-pass-plugin={PLUGIN}", "-passes=cq-lower", *o["kflags"],
                   *([] if lowered.suffix == ".bc" else ["-S"]), "-o", lowered]
        with open(linked, "rb") as fin:
            run(opt_cmd, "opt -passes=cq-lower", stdin=fin)

        # 4. Output.
        out = Path(o["out"])
        staged = tmp / ("staged" + out.suffix)
        if o["mode"] == "S" or (o["mode"] == "c" and o["emit_llvm"]):
            shutil.copyfile(lowered, staged)
        elif o["mode"] == "c":
            obj = tmp / (out.stem + ".o") if out.suffix == ".a" else staged
            # A lowered library is megabytes of straight-line calls: -O1 code generation spends minutes in register
            # allocation there (61 s of a 70 s stdlib build), -O0 seconds.
            run([tool("clang"), "-O0" if o["lib"] else "-O1", "-Xclang", "-disable-llvm-passes", "-c", "-x", "ir", lowered,
                 "-o", obj], "clang -c of the lowered module")
            if out.suffix == ".a":
                run([tool("llvm-ar"), "rcs", staged, obj], "llvm-ar of the lowered library")
        else:
            objs = [p for p in o["inputs"] if p.suffix in LINK_SUFFIXES]
            # Rulings Q7: the host symbols are one runtime object linked after the pass, never lowered; only when the
            # lowered module asks for one (a module the pass left as it was needs no bus and no backend).
            undefined = nm(lowered, ["--undefined-only"], "llvm-nm of the lowered module", tmp)
            # A root list means a lowered library is linked: it asks for them whatever the program does.
            if listed or {n.removeprefix("_") for n in undefined} & HOST_SYMBOLS:   # Mach-O spells C names with a leading _
                host_obj = tmp / "cq_host.o"
                run([tool("clang"), "-O1", "-c", HOST_SOURCE, "-o", host_obj], "clang -c of bundle/host/cq_host.c")
                objs.insert(0, host_obj)
            # The float templates are the compiler's: its lowered SoftFloat archives go last, so a template the
            # backend defines itself is the backend's and the library supplies the rest.
            floats = [p for p in FLOAT_LIBS if p.exists()] if o["softfloat"] else []
            run([tool("clang"), "-O1", "-Xclang", "-disable-llvm-passes", "-x", "ir", lowered, "-x", "none",
                 *objs, *o["backend"], *floats, *(["-lc++"] if any(p.suffix in CXX_SUFFIXES for p in o["inputs"]) else []),
                 # cq_host.c's weak import of the backend's optional cqrt_qram_object, _unbound and _pointer (BACKEND_ABI §1.10, Objects)
                 *(["-Wl,-U,_cqrt_qram_object", "-Wl,-U,_cqrt_qram_unbound", "-Wl,-U,_cqrt_qram_pointer"] if sys.platform == "darwin" else []), "-o", staged], "link of the lowered program")

        # 5. --cq-check: the C-oracle check of cq-w1-usercheck on this program.
        status = 0
        if o["check"]:
            o1 = linked
            low_ll = lowered
            if lowered.suffix == ".bc":
                low_ll = work / "lowered.ll"
                run([tool("llvm-dis"), lowered, "-o", low_ll], "llvm-dis of the lowered module")
            cmd = [sys.executable, "-m", "cqcheck", "user", "--o1", o1.resolve(), "--lowered", low_ll.resolve(),
                   "--entry", o["entry"]]
            if o["samples"] is not None:
                cmd += ["--samples", o["samples"]]
            if VERBOSE:
                print(" ".join(map(str, cmd)), file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
            env = dict(os.environ)
            if listed and not o["lib"]:
                # Rule 27 (owner ruling 2026-11-20): a listed function the program calls only with classical actuals and no
                # QUANTUM cell is its C symbol's call, rule 16's like an unlisted callee's: the checker's stand-in only for
                # a name the lowered program calls through no host call or effect entry.
                text = Path(low_ll).read_text()
                stand = [n for n in listed if not re.search(rf'@\.cq\.effect\.{re.escape(n)}\b|call [^\n]*@"?(\\01_)?{re.escape(n)}"?\(', text)]
                env["CQ_ROOTS_EXTRA"] = ",".join(filter(None, [env.get("CQ_ROOTS_EXTRA", ""), *stand]))
            status = subprocess.run([str(c) for c in cmd], cwd=ROOT / "checker", env=env).returncode
            if status != 0:
                print(f"cqcc: --cq-check: cqcheck user exited {status}", file=sys.stderr)

        shutil.move(str(staged), str(out))
        return status


if __name__ == "__main__":
    try:
        sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
    except DriverError as e:
        print(e, file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(e.status)
